From b43164cd8f1452200891380ba384d0a0e88fc4df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:56:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: move a compressed gui off the only plane the
 video can use

The gui surface takes the first modifier the GBM implementation picks
from the output plane formats, which can be a compressed one such as
Arm AFBC. Its plane is then the only one that scans out that modifier.
When the video is also compressed and only that plane accepts it, as
with AFBC video on the RK3566 cluster window, no video plane is found
and DRM PRIME rendering fails.

When that is the case and a linear gui would leave a plane for the
video, recreate the gui surface with a linear layout, move the gui to a
plane that scans it out, and look for the video plane again. The gui
stays linear for the rest of the session.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
